body:
When reviewing https://github.com/soda-inria/tabicl/pull/157 I realized that feature grouping might cause detrimental colisions for datasets with small number of features.

It might be interesting to investigate if:

- it is possible to craft adversarial ML tasks that would fail because of this;
- predictive performance actually degrades on a set of say 10 benchmark ML tasks with small numbers of features;
- automatically disabling feature grouping can help on such datasets;
- alternatively if a pretraining with disabled feature grouping on tables with small numbers of columns would be needed for a future pretraining run.
